  "text": "proprium.commemoratio-omnium-fidelium-defunctorum-missa-iii-evangelium",
  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed — Mass III” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, Jesus said to the crowds of the Jews: “I am the living bread, who came down from heaven. If anyone eats of this bread, he will live forever; and the bread which I shall give is My Flesh, for the life of the world.” The Jews therefore disputed among themselves, saying: “How can this man give us His Flesh to eat?” Then Jesus said to them: “Amen, amen, I say to you: unless you eat the Flesh of the Son of Man and drink His Blood, you will not have life within you. Whoever eats My Flesh and drinks My Blood has eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.”" }
